module gunbc.plans.flex_supplier_generalization

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetirement, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock, TableBlock, AlignNone }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { h2, p, li, ul, ol, cell, row }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn flex_supplier_generalization_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "Plan, no actuation (operator request 2026-10-23): add AWS EC2 g7e / RTX PRO 6000 Server, spot first and on-demand separately priced, as a second flex supplier row. No AWS launch without separate operator go-ahead. [Original declaration census and decision receipts](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/3e5a0f1f0dbc62e0d3589df44146858d3147c9e9/dag/gunbc/plans/flex_supplier_generalization.dag)."),
    h2(text: "One supplier interface, existing policy and selection"),
    p(text: "Keep product.fabric.flex_policy, generic FlexBidAttempt, flex_bid_admission, flex_market card ranking/release and product.fabric.selection.select_supply over CandidateOffer with AvailabilityObservation. FlexMachineKey already includes provider DeclarationRef + account + machine. Generalize the root; never fork flex_aws_* loops, add a supplier enum to the hub, or add a second chooser. Vast’s bid-level learner is supplier pricing, not generic spot policy."),
    p(text: "FlexSupplierRow binds five agnostic roles, with realization dispatch peripheral: screened candidates for the ONE serving recipe; price rule; complete paginated owned roster; typed create/release requests; settlement observation. Every supplier screens disk/VRAM/driver/RAM/TP, preserves cross-supplier machine mismatch refusal, and maps ownership from its own label/tag. Union the rosters before fleet cap/release/cleanup so caps are fleet-wide. Complete roster seals, page folds and id uniqueness remain required."),
    p(text: "The least rented carriers are RentedInstanceObserved { id, owner_label } and RentedDestroyRequest { instance_id }; the later consumer derivation supersedes the earlier speculative status field. Delete unused provider_ask, do not generalize a Vast pre-actuation machine into an EC2 post-answer identity. Pending-create standing stays supplier-local (Vast FlexCreateStanding; AWS client token). Vast destroy moves to flex_vast_destroy_perform and resolves only among our label in the complete roster. #14879 landed that carrier/destroy portion; the FlexSupplierRow fold and Vast row remain the next 4a step. Preserve receipt lines and flex_vast_loop_witness/flex_vast_shadow_witness. Host enrollment maps when AWS needs it; Vast settlement remains its charges walk."),
    h2(text: "AWS selection and hard constraints"),
    p(text: "D1 decided RunInstances, one selected candidate per call, from a per-recipe launch template: spot one-time, interruption terminate, MaxPrice = admitted rate, owner TagSpecifications. CreateFleet must not hide another allocation strategy. A candidate is region × AZ × size × layout × spot/on-demand; layout declares independent replicas, one TP=N replica, or billed idle GPUs. Read cited/versioned GPU count, vCPU, RAM, NVMe and network from upstream instance types, never infer them from a family name."),
    p(text: "Spot price is the latest fresh DescribeSpotPriceHistory point for type/AZ/Linux-UNIX; missing/stale refuses FlexMarketPriceUnobserved. Spot is not the Vast bid market. On-demand is a separate LIVE Price List GetProducts candidate and FlexOnDemandReference, not static M7a pricing or an actuation fallback. Capacity refusals (InsufficientInstanceCapacity/MaxSpotInstanceCountExceeded) return to the next pass with the candidate excluded."),
    p(text: "Exclude before Pareto: recipe RAM floor (26.8 GiB randomly read unswappable PLE table plus overhead), local instance-store NVMe mounted at /cache, single-instance TP width, and quota. Never EBS for the LMCache L2 tier; extra RAM/NVMe above floors are priced axes. Quota uses account-wide running AND pending/open requests across all workloads plus candidate vCPUs against the applied regional G/VT spot or on-demand quota. Read paginated Service Quotas and CloudWatch AWS/Usage; unread usage refuses, zero quota excludes."),
    p(text: "Objective is delivered-token cost via serving_recipe.serving_cost_per_million_tokens → serving_unit_cost_for_selection, which refuses Estimated/unread costs; no GPU-hour substitute and no latency axis. PR4 must first widen throughput identity beyond recipe to recipe + instance type + topology + replica/TP layout + host/cache realization. With observed rate R, delivered throughput T, lifetime L and startup S, use R*L/(3600*T*(L-S)) plus interrupted re-prefill and re-tuning losses. T and L must be READ before ranking. Startup is launch→first token per region/size; 3–5 minute warm and 15–25 minute cold figures are bets. Own launch→notice/termination observations establish lifetime; Spot Advisor bands only order probes. On-demand uses the same startup and policy-bounded lifetime. Apply a per-pool concentration policy limit as a hard constraint on EVERY new candidate: exclude a full region/AZ pool for that pass. This spreads near-equal prices within the existing switch premium, without another chooser."),
    h2(text: "Shared image, weights, cache and credential path"),
    p(text: "PR3a #14866 owns supplier-agnostic flex_serving_image: driver 580+, Docker/NVIDIA toolkit, pinned image digest, shared flex_vast_onstart. CopyImage/read AMI per region. Generalize existing ServingWeightsSource / RentedWeightsPlacement from ninfer/R2 to pinned Hugging Face revision and per-region S3 locator, resolved via SSM rather than bucket literals. Copy weights in parallel to NVMe; no Mountpoint lazy read, EBS weights or FSR substitute."),
    p(text: "Cache key must cover GPU model, driver, image digest, model revision, recipe/TP and verified runtime/profile derivation before trust. Observed lil-serve layout puts HF weights under HF_HOME/hub and JIT under runtime-lock/profile hash, which omits GPU/driver; Server and Workstation share rtx-pro-6000-pcie. Until source verifies the complete derivation, use observed directory plus GPU/driver/image: over-separation is acceptable, over-sharing is not. Redirect HF hub to NVMe."),
    p(text: "Use extdeps.docker.cli.DockerCreateSpec: all GPUs, host IPC, image shm, /cache and HF hub binds at /root/.cache/huggingface, image PORT, root-only env-file for POOL_API_KEY, unless-stopped restart, bash entrypoint running shared onstart then wait (onstart backgrounds the server). Add real env-file/entrypoint fields to that owner, not scripted docker flags."),
    p(text: "One counted RetainedShellScript pre-step, with reason and typed-host-effect dissolution target: RAID0 multiple NVMe devices and mount /cache, refuse absence; IMDSv2 region/instance ID; parallel pinned S3 copy; complete-key cache fetch requiring a sentinel written last; bounded SSM poll or typed/logged timeout; root-only env file; container start. Only after /health succeeds on a cache miss publish /cache/jit and the sentinel last. AWS selects the pre-step, Vast none. User-data combines it with rendered docker create/start argv; template requires IMDSv2. PR3b follows #14862/#14866."),
    p(text: "Every placement checks every pinned qwen3_8_flash_next_files entry: size plus HubFileDigest LFS SHA-256 or git-blob SHA-1, with no extra/missing files. Refuse corruption before serving; an unverified bucket copy is not the pin. The receipt checked 14 small git blobs and the smallest LFS file, each with a one-byte RED. AMI also needs git hash-object and mdadm."),
    p(text: "Credential delivery is DECIDED SSM (2026-10-23): loop writes KMS-encrypted SecureString after RunInstances yields instance ID, keyed to it; instance reads once with bounded poll, loop deletes on enrollment. No secret in user-data, tags, console or argv. Residual: role reads the flex prefix, so overlapping boot windows expose another owned rental’s key. ec2:SourceInstanceARN is documented as a condition key, not the proposed Resource policy variable; per-instance policy would grant the loop iam:PutRolePolicy, which is not chosen."),
    h2(text: "Interruption, billing and isolation"),
    p(text: "Two-minute IMDS spot/instance-action / EventBridge notice is best effort. Drain stops new turns, release allocation, observe termination. PR4 must choose before building: EventBridge rule/target read by the loop with modeled payload, or onstart IMDS polling reporting through enrollment. DescribeInstances alone does not observe notice. A roster finding shutting-down/terminated without notice releases and separately counts unannounced reclaim. Lost KV means re-prefill cost/latency, not correctness loss. Two minutes is below flex_reconstruction’s 300-second window, so this is hard loss, not graceful migration."),
    p(text: "D2: Apply need not await billing, but settlement remains typed/countable RentedSettlementUnobserved under a gunbc.rung_drop row filed with PR4. Restore it only with AWS billing observations joined by instance ID. Conservative liability = max(admitted spot price, MaxPrice) × billed time, per second from running with one-minute minimum per start, ending at shutting-down; never zero. Vast retains observed charges."),
    p(text: "D3: no dedicated account. Owner-tag IAM restricts launch/terminate; flex_policy refuses projected liability above its parameterized ceiling. Separately AWS Budgets attaches deny-RunInstances to the flex principal at the cap, using an activated cost-allocation owner tag and execution role. Lagging Budgets is a backstop, never primary accounting. Budget amount is operator policy, not a corpus literal. Operator confirmed credits cover spot."),
    h2(text: "Model-first delivery and operator actions"),
    p(text: "PR2 grounds EC2 API 2016-11-15 requests/responses (Run/Terminate/DescribeInstances pagination, prices/types, launch templates/versions, interruption), instance-type facts, AWS Price List live query, Service Quotas and Budgets in independently versioned extdeps homes. IAM policy belongs beside credential custody, not upstream facts. D4 chose AWS CLI v2 JSON: own pinned/versioned CLI model projecting EC2 shapes; interface calls with peripheral handler so a later curl-SigV4/XML handler is a row swap; custody-host environment or 0600 credentials only, never debug; explicit region on every call."),
    p(text: "Operator provides principal/custody and modeled PolicyDocument: ec2 RunInstances/CreateTags-on-create/TerminateInstances, DescribeInstances/Types/SpotPriceHistory/Images/Regions/InstanceTypeOfferings, Create/DescribeLaunchTemplate and Version, CopyImage; pricing:GetProducts; Service Quotas GetServiceQuota/ListServiceQuotas; AMI ssm:GetParameter; loop PutParameter/DeleteParameter + kms:Encrypt; instance GetParameter + kms:Decrypt; iam:PassRole for that role. Scope region and RequestTag/ResourceTag where supported. Instance role gets weights S3 GetObject/ListBucket and tuning-prefix PutObject only, not the loop principal. No iam:PutRolePolicy is implied."),
    p(text: "Operator raises G/VT spot and on-demand vCPU quotas where policy should reach. Regions are not fixed: Plan reads offered regions and applied quota/account usage; that output informs quota actions. Custody reuses pinned SecretRef version/host/path, with no key in corpus. Public source must not add account IDs, private endpoints or operator-specific buying prices; observe AWS account at runtime rather than repeating the existing public Vast account row."),
    p(text: "4a first runs the Vast row behavior-preservingly; 4b adds AWS read-only Plan observations (regions/offerings/quotas/types/prices/owned roster) and screened walls. Absent credentials refuse typed, not an empty supply field. Current flex_pass_run has NO intent and leaves flex_select_supply_consumer_frontier open. Wiring select_supply over the union closes it once for both suppliers. AWS Apply is a separate operator go-ahead, not implied by a green Plan pass."),
  ]
}

data flex_supplier_generalization_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "flex-supplier-generalization",
  title: "Flex autoscaler: Vast and AWS EC2 as supplier rows",
  body: flex_supplier_generalization_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Retires when the flex loop selects over supplier rows with Vast and AWS EC2 as inhabitants, no flex symbol outside a supplier row names an extdeps.cloud.vast_ai type, and the AWS row runs its Plan-mode pass green by execution.") }
}
